275 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 276 0 R/Alt(Three panels. (a) Acceleration in g against time from minus 20 to 100 ms: a small slow swing before zero, then a dense oscillation from about 3 to 55 ms reaching about plus 7.7 and minus 9.4 g, then small slow swings to 100 ms. (b) Acceleration against time from minus 80 to 80 ms: an orange solid half-sine peaking near 2.05 g at zero and a green dashed terminal-peak sawtooth peaking near 2.37 g just after zero, both preceded and followed by shallow negative compensation half-sines of about minus 0.2 g between about minus 60 and 60 ms. (c) A log-log plot of the SRS in g against natural frequency from 10 to 2000 Hz: the target rises from about 0.1 g at 10 Hz to about 15 g near 60 Hz and stays between about 14 and 22 g to 2000 Hz, inside a blue inner band and a wider gray outer band.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[30]/Pg 755 0 R>>
endobj
